# Done-markers are run state, not record: they tell a detached run's dead shell that it
# finished. Tracking them means a rerun shows a phantom deletion in the shared tree's
# porcelain, and a committed marker asserts "this finished" about a run that may be
# mid-flight. The logs beside them are the record. (Swept in by an unrelated lane's bare
# commit at 5c7ad74; untracked here.)
*.DONE

# The ladder-witness snapshots: insurance taken out after a peer's log was truncated
# mid-campaign and erased rows this lane had cited. It never paid out -- the rerun was
# committed intact (5ebaf16) and every witnessed row is present there, verified by
# comparison, so tracking these would put a duplicate of a committed artifact into the
# record. Kept on disk, out of the record, same rule as the done-markers above.
witness/
